NNAAMMEE
     mmaakkeeddbbmm — create a YP database

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmaakkeeddbbmm [--bbllssUUuu] [--dd _y_p___d_o_m_a_i_n___n_a_m_e] [--ii _y_p___i_n_p_u_t___f_i_l_e]
             [--mm _y_p___m_a_s_t_e_r___n_a_m_e] [--oo _y_p___o_u_t_p_u_t___f_i_l_e] _i_n_f_i_l_e _o_u_t_f_i_l_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmaakkeeddbbmm is the utility in YP that creates the database file containing
     the YP map.  The database format is a slightly modified version of ndbm.

     The options are as follows:

     --bb      Interdomain.  Include an entry in the database informing a YP
             server to use DNS to get information about unknown hosts.  This
             option will only have effect on the two maps hosts.byname and
             hosts.byaddr.

     --dd _y_p___d_o_m_a_i_n___n_a_m_e
             Include an entry in the map with the key YP_DOMAIN_NAME and the
             argument as value.

     --ii _y_p___i_n_p_u_t___f_i_l_e
             Include an entry in the map with the key YP_INPUT_FILE and the
             argument as value.

     --ll      Lowercase.  Convert all keys to lower case before adding them to
             the YP database.

     --mm _y_p___m_a_s_t_e_r___n_a_m_e
             Include an entry in the map with the key YP_MASTER_NAME and the
             argument as value.

     --oo _y_p___o_u_t_p_u_t___f_i_l_e
             Include an entry in the map with the key YP_OUTPUT_FILE and the
             argument as value.

     --ss      Secure map.  Include an entry in the database informing ypxfr(8)
             and ypserv(8) that the YP map is going to be handled as secure.

     --UU      Same as --uu but also try the hash(3) format.

     --uu      Dump a database to standard output.

